  A trucker is transporting canaries cross-country in a closed trailer.
He gets to a bridge that says, "8 Tons Or Less."  His truck, with all
the caged canaries in the back, weighs just over 8 tons.  So he gets
out of the truck, takes a baseball bat and beats on the side of the
truck so that all the canaries flap up in the air.  Then he gets back
in the truck and drives halfway across the bridge. :)
  [The weight of the flying canaries doesn't disappear; it's transferred
down the column of air to the bed of the truck.  The truck's weight
does not change one iota.]

  I think that the code should be changed so that small creatures
do not set off squeaky-board traps, and possibly so that legless
non-flying creatures (i.e., snakes) *never* set them off.  Can anyone
with a pet snake confirm or disprove that snakes don't squeak? :)
  I think flying large creatures such as gargoyles *should* set off
squeaky-board traps, by the force of their weight.  Only really
"weightless" creatures such as wraiths and ghosts should be immune
from those traps.

  I'd really like to see a patch for this, if I've understood the
current behavior correctly -- it seems really wrong the way it is.

